    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Didar Ali, a student at AKU's Faculty of Arts and Sciences, still clearly remembers the terror brought on by the 2010 floods that destroyed his village in Gilgit-Baltistan's Ghizer district. He was a young child at the time, but he remembers seeing homes, agricultural crops, and roads swept away as rivers swelled and burst. \"Climate crises would wreak havoc year after year,\" he recalls. \"People in my village would just say, 'This is the will of God. There's nothing we can do.'\"",
